module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.Completion.BaseIdealKoszulGenerators
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.GlobalSectionsCompletionKoszulIdentity

/-!
# The identity of Tag 0BLX at the ideal sheaf of an ideal of the base ring

Let `A` be a ring, `f : X ⟶ Spec A` a scheme over `A` and `a_1, …, a_r ∈ A`. The identity

`RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` in `D(A)`

of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], proved on a ringed site at an ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global
sections of `𝒪` (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite`
`.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections`), is read here at the small Zariski site
of `X` and at the ideal sheaf generated by the images `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` of the chosen elements,
the ring map `Stacks.Algebraization.baseSiteRingHom` making `𝒪_X` a sheaf of `A`-algebras.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections_baseSiteRingHom`:
  the identity, for an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪_X)`.

## Implementation notes

This is one application of one theorem, and it has a module of its own for an elaboration reason.
The theorem applied carries two completeness conditions as instance hypotheses — the countable
coproduct of the Koszul system in `D(𝒪_X)` and the countable product of the Hom tower — and both
are found by instance search here, in a closure that holds the ringed-site Koszul material and
nothing else. In the larger closure of
`Completion/GeneralCohomologyAdicCompletion.lean`, which also holds the schemes-level completion
material, the search for the coproduct exhausts its heartbeats. Isolating the application keeps
the search small; the statement is also written out rather than left to unification, so that the
two conditions are synthesized against a known goal.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (opensRingedSite)
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of A)) {r : ℕ}
  (a : Fin r → A)

/-- **The identity `RΓ(𝒞, K)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, K^∧)` of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX]** at the ideal sheaf generated
by the images `ρ a_1, …, ρ a_r` of a finite family of elements of `A`, in the ringed-site
spelling. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections` at the small
Zariski site of `X`, with the ring map `Stacks.Algebraization.baseSiteRingHom` making `𝒪_X` a
sheaf of `A`-algebras.

The statement is spelled out rather than left to unification so that the countable coproduct of
the Koszul system and the countable product of the Hom tower, which that theorem carries as
instance hypotheses, are synthesized against a known goal. -/
theorem nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections_baseSiteRingHom
    (K : DerivedCategory X.Modules) :
    Nonempty
      ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded
          (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) A (baseSiteRingHom f)).obj
          ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
            (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf
              (fun i ↦ AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSections
                (baseSiteRingHom f (a i))))).obj K) ≅
        (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor A a).obj
          ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOverUnbounded
            (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) A (baseSiteRingHom f)).obj K)) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections
    (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) A (baseSiteRingHom f) a K

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
